    Bug 2016161 - Part 4: Extend content script tests in browser_ext_contentScripts.js. r=darktrojan


    While investigating our remaining content script tests in `browser_ext_contentScripts.js`
    we learned that it is only testing tabs which have been created by Thunderbird itself via
    `window.openContentTab()`. This is insufficient and needs to be extended to also test tabs
    and popups which have been created by the WebExtension API.

    This patch refactors the test to de-duplicate code and extend its testing capabilities to
    WebExtension tabs and popups, while injecting content scripts into web-pages and also into
    `about:blank`.

    The triggering principal used by the tabs API is fixed in the same way as the first patch
    in this stack is fixing it for the windows API, allowing the updated test to pass when
    injecting into `about:blank`.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D283247

